1
00:00:44,294 --> 00:00:45,503
Listen.

2
00:00:45,587 --> 00:00:48,465
You don't throw shuriken. You shoot them.

3
00:00:50,091 --> 00:00:51,092
Now!

4
00:00:53,845 --> 00:00:55,263
Well…

5
00:00:55,930 --> 00:00:58,725
everyone's suited to different things.

6
00:01:05,899 --> 00:01:07,650
Let's get the situation straight.

7
00:01:10,070 --> 00:01:14,157
After leaving Sunpu Castle,
Ieyasu has entered Nijo Castle in Kyoto.

8
00:01:14,240 --> 00:01:17,869
His goal is clear: destroy Osaka Castle,

9
00:01:17,952 --> 00:01:20,246
crush the Toyotomi, and unite the realm.

10
00:01:20,330 --> 00:01:21,623
What about Hidetada's army?

11
00:01:21,706 --> 00:01:23,333
They've already left Edo.

12
00:01:23,416 --> 00:01:24,876
When will they join up?

13
00:01:24,959 --> 00:01:26,044
In about eight days.

14
00:01:26,127 --> 00:01:29,756
If we launch a surprise attack on Kyoto
before their forces assemble,

15
00:01:29,839 --> 00:01:31,132
we might win.

16
00:01:31,216 --> 00:01:33,009
That's Lord Yukimura's plan.

17
00:01:33,092 --> 00:01:34,886
And Lady Yodo rejected it.

18
00:01:35,553 --> 00:01:38,389
Lady Yodo is the castle's de facto ruler.

19
00:01:39,307 --> 00:01:40,683
We can't defy her.

20
00:01:41,267 --> 00:01:44,938
But a siege puts us
at a disadvantage, doesn't it?

21
00:01:45,021 --> 00:01:46,815
Not necessarily.

22
00:01:47,690 --> 00:01:49,442
If we can expect reinforcements,

23
00:01:49,526 --> 00:01:52,570
we can hold out until they arrive
and trap the enemy in a pincer attack.

24
00:01:53,071 --> 00:01:55,865
We should assume no daimyo
will side with the Toyotomi.

25
00:01:56,407 --> 00:01:58,201
It would be suicide.

26
00:02:00,120 --> 00:02:02,956
The gap between ideal and reality…

27
00:02:03,039 --> 00:02:06,668
Why aren't we allowed to attend
the war council in the first place?

28
00:02:07,168 --> 00:02:13,424
Everyone in this castle looks down on us
as scum with no loyalty.

29
00:02:14,092 --> 00:02:19,139
Must a ninja endure such treatment?

30
00:02:19,764 --> 00:02:24,936
Then why not use Saizo's transformation
technique to impersonate Lady Yodo?

31
00:02:25,019 --> 00:02:27,856
We could tie up
the real Lady Yodo somewhere…

32
00:02:27,939 --> 00:02:30,191
We'd all be beheaded if we did that.

33
00:02:30,275 --> 00:02:33,820
Besides, Saizo can't imitate
a woman's mannerisms.

34
00:02:35,488 --> 00:02:37,365
You don't know women, huh?

35
00:02:37,448 --> 00:02:38,533
Shut up, you stupid monkey!

36
00:02:38,616 --> 00:02:40,160
What's that supposed to mean?

37
00:02:40,243 --> 00:02:41,369
Don't make things up!

38
00:02:41,452 --> 00:02:44,247
-It's because you…
-Both of you, enough!

39
00:02:44,330 --> 00:02:45,874
Then I'll transform into her.

40
00:02:45,957 --> 00:02:47,375
As if a fool like you could.

41
00:02:47,959 --> 00:02:49,752
Yes I can!

42
00:02:50,503 --> 00:02:51,337
Hey!

43
00:02:54,007 --> 00:02:55,216
Excuse me.

44
00:03:01,723 --> 00:03:04,934
Lord Yukimura,
Lady Yodo requests your presence.

45
00:03:05,018 --> 00:03:05,977
I'll be right there.

46
00:03:09,355 --> 00:03:10,815
I'm counting on you, old man.

47
00:03:11,566 --> 00:03:12,400
Sure.

48
00:03:14,444 --> 00:03:16,237
Come on, you go, too.

49
00:03:17,071 --> 00:03:19,240
-What?
-We're gathering intel.

50
00:03:19,782 --> 00:03:21,701
You want to get strong
like a ninja, right?

51
00:03:22,535 --> 00:03:23,369
Yes!

52
00:03:28,708 --> 00:03:29,876
I've brought him, my lady.

53
00:03:42,180 --> 00:03:45,600
I, Sanada Yukimura, have arrived.

54
00:03:46,392 --> 00:03:47,268
Well?

55
00:03:47,810 --> 00:03:49,938
How does it feel to be back
after 20 years?

56
00:03:53,942 --> 00:03:56,694
It brings back many memories.

57
00:03:58,363 --> 00:03:59,530
Is that all?

58
00:04:17,173 --> 00:04:20,635
At the war council earlier,
I spoke harshly to you.

59
00:04:21,636 --> 00:04:23,012
You must have taken offense.

60
00:04:24,764 --> 00:04:25,890
Not at all.

61
00:04:26,391 --> 00:04:28,309
Don't speak so formally.

62
00:04:29,894 --> 00:04:31,646
Hold me tight…

63
00:04:32,939 --> 00:04:34,232
like you used to…

64
00:04:37,110 --> 00:04:38,027
Lady Yodo.

65
00:04:38,945 --> 00:04:39,862
I beseech you

66
00:04:40,571 --> 00:04:42,573
to reconsider.

67
00:04:44,242 --> 00:04:46,119
With our provisions limited,

68
00:04:47,620 --> 00:04:48,705
a siege would…

69
00:04:48,788 --> 00:04:50,915
We've settled that matter already.

70
00:04:53,084 --> 00:04:54,127
All I ask

71
00:04:55,211 --> 00:04:58,172
is that you protect Hideyori.

72
00:05:01,592 --> 00:05:03,678
He's grown, hasn't he?

73
00:05:05,346 --> 00:05:06,514
His looks…

74
00:05:09,100 --> 00:05:12,186
and courage may not quite
match yours, though.

75
00:05:14,480 --> 00:05:15,398
So he is…

76
00:05:22,697 --> 00:05:23,698
Lord Hideyori is…

77
00:05:25,825 --> 00:05:27,076
He's your son.

78
00:05:36,002 --> 00:05:39,589
Would you risk Hideyori's life
by sending him into battle?

79
00:05:40,298 --> 00:05:42,300
You expect me to accept that
as his mother?

80
00:05:45,511 --> 00:05:47,972
Never again speak of a plan

81
00:05:49,182 --> 00:05:50,808
that would put my son in danger.

82
00:06:22,215 --> 00:06:24,133
SOBA

83
00:06:24,217 --> 00:06:26,052
It'd be nice to open a shop like this.

84
00:06:26,135 --> 00:06:27,303
Yeah.

85
00:06:28,429 --> 00:06:29,931
You could open an apothecary.

86
00:06:30,598 --> 00:06:31,599
And I could open…

87
00:06:33,142 --> 00:06:34,143
a restaurant?

88
00:06:34,227 --> 00:06:35,937
You could do it, Brother!

89
00:06:36,521 --> 00:06:37,396
Really?

90
00:06:37,897 --> 00:06:39,398
I've gotta get my act together.

91
00:06:41,442 --> 00:06:42,318
All right!

92
00:06:43,194 --> 00:06:47,907
Two bowls, coming up!
Here you go. Thanks as always.

93
00:06:49,534 --> 00:06:52,203
We're full right now,
so please wait over there.

94
00:06:52,286 --> 00:06:53,996
-Orin, one sake, please.
-Orin…

95
00:06:54,497 --> 00:06:55,414
SWEET SHOP

96
00:06:55,498 --> 00:06:56,582
Thank you!

97
00:06:56,666 --> 00:06:58,042
Thank you.

98
00:06:59,794 --> 00:07:02,213
So this is konpeito.

99
00:07:02,296 --> 00:07:03,131
Yeah.

100
00:07:03,714 --> 00:07:04,924
Sweet…

101
00:07:05,007 --> 00:07:07,009
Don't "Sweet…" me!

102
00:07:07,093 --> 00:07:08,761
What the hell are you doing here, Saizo?!

103
00:07:08,845 --> 00:07:09,846
LOCAL SPECIALTY
KONPEITO

104
00:07:09,929 --> 00:07:11,431
You promised, didn't you?

105
00:07:12,098 --> 00:07:16,352
If I brought you to Osaka, I'd get
three gold coins from old Yukimura.

106
00:07:16,436 --> 00:07:18,271
And Yuri and I would have konpeito.

107
00:07:18,354 --> 00:07:19,647
I never said just the two of us.

108
00:07:19,730 --> 00:07:20,648
Yuri!

109
00:07:20,731 --> 00:07:21,607
What a scam…

110
00:07:22,316 --> 00:07:23,401
Hey!

111
00:07:24,277 --> 00:07:25,319
Konpeito scam!

112
00:07:25,403 --> 00:07:27,321
Don't waste your energy shouting.

113
00:07:28,072 --> 00:07:32,702
Until Lord Yukimura comes up
with a new plan, we need to rest.

114
00:07:39,709 --> 00:07:42,545
By the way, have any of you
ever seen Lord Hideyori?

115
00:07:43,921 --> 00:07:44,797
No.

116
00:07:45,756 --> 00:07:47,884
Want me to show you something interesting?

117
00:07:48,593 --> 00:07:52,513
So Lady Yodo still won't reconsider…

118
00:07:54,891 --> 00:07:55,933
I'm sorry.

119
00:07:56,517 --> 00:07:58,811
You have nothing
to apologize for, my lord.

120
00:07:58,895 --> 00:07:59,729
Anayama!

121
00:08:00,396 --> 00:08:04,442
We'll find a way to defeat the Tokugawa
while holding out in the castle.

122
00:08:06,068 --> 00:08:08,821
I've been thinking all day!

123
00:08:09,447 --> 00:08:12,116
What about you, Mochizuki?
Where have you been wandering off to?

124
00:08:14,410 --> 00:08:16,120
You went to see your daughter, didn't you?

125
00:08:17,830 --> 00:08:19,624
You knew?

126
00:08:20,583 --> 00:08:23,878
You mean,
the one you left behind in Osaka?

127
00:08:25,213 --> 00:08:27,381
I couldn't tell her I was her father.

128
00:08:28,007 --> 00:08:31,844
If I told her, I'd only cause her trouble.

129
00:08:32,512 --> 00:08:35,598
Still… when you know she's right there,

130
00:08:36,474 --> 00:08:38,267
you can't help rushing to see her.

131
00:08:39,185 --> 00:08:40,228
Yeah.

132
00:08:42,480 --> 00:08:44,148
"Can't help rushing to her"?

133
00:08:47,944 --> 00:08:48,778
That's it!

134
00:08:51,989 --> 00:08:55,451
I've found the secret
to defeating the Tokugawa.

135
00:09:07,255 --> 00:09:08,965
He's not just similar…

136
00:09:10,675 --> 00:09:12,677
He's the spitting image of him.

137
00:09:12,760 --> 00:09:16,389
I've come with a new plan.

138
00:09:17,348 --> 00:09:18,933
There's no need for a plan.

139
00:09:19,433 --> 00:09:21,519
We've already decided
to hold out in the castle.

140
00:09:22,103 --> 00:09:23,229
Then, Lord Ono,

141
00:09:23,938 --> 00:09:26,774
where do you think
the Tokugawa army will attack from?

142
00:09:28,526 --> 00:09:29,735
Well…

143
00:09:31,904 --> 00:09:33,447
If I knew that, I wouldn't be…

144
00:09:33,531 --> 00:09:34,365
The south.

145
00:09:36,701 --> 00:09:41,122
I'm afraid the southern defenses
of Osaka Castle are weak.

146
00:09:41,789 --> 00:09:44,458
Are you saying this castle has a weakness?

147
00:09:44,542 --> 00:09:46,335
Don't speak carelessly.

148
00:09:47,670 --> 00:09:52,633
There's high ground to the south,
the coast west, and a river north.

149
00:09:52,717 --> 00:09:56,178
If I were Ieyasu,
I'd attack from the south.

150
00:09:56,262 --> 00:10:00,975
Then we must build a fortified outpost
in the southeast to repel the Tokugawa.

151
00:10:01,058 --> 00:10:01,934
An outpost?

152
00:10:02,935 --> 00:10:06,480
With an outpost, we can delay the enemy
and dictate their route.

153
00:10:06,981 --> 00:10:09,317
Even if Ieyasu brings a huge army,

154
00:10:09,400 --> 00:10:12,028
if he bypasses it,
we'll strike from behind.

155
00:10:12,862 --> 00:10:17,199
He can't ignore it
and will have to send troops there?

156
00:10:18,242 --> 00:10:19,160
Exactly.

157
00:10:19,785 --> 00:10:21,621
Harunaga, is that true?

158
00:10:22,455 --> 00:10:25,207
Lord Sanada's prediction that
Ieyasu will attack from the south

159
00:10:25,291 --> 00:10:27,335
is just speculation, isn't it?

160
00:10:28,336 --> 00:10:31,631
We'll deliberately thin out our troops
in the south, except at the outpost.

161
00:10:32,632 --> 00:10:36,010
There's no way Ieyasu will overlook that.
He'll take the bait.

162
00:10:37,511 --> 00:10:41,182
But who will man the outpost?

163
00:10:41,974 --> 00:10:45,186
About 200 of the Sanada clan's retainers.

164
00:10:45,853 --> 00:10:48,856
We'll station ninja there, too.

165
00:10:49,857 --> 00:10:52,485
What can a mere 200 men do?

166
00:10:53,069 --> 00:10:55,029
Two hundred elite warriors

167
00:10:56,197 --> 00:10:57,740
who drove the Tokugawa back at Ueda.

168
00:11:01,369 --> 00:11:02,912
Just as I'd expect from Lord Yukimura.

169
00:11:03,913 --> 00:11:06,832
Will you approve the construction
of the outpost?

170
00:11:06,916 --> 00:11:11,921
I can build a fort
that will defeat the Tokugawa.

171
00:11:12,588 --> 00:11:13,547
Wait.

172
00:11:14,548 --> 00:11:18,719
Can we really trust Lord Sanada's plan?

173
00:11:20,388 --> 00:11:21,555
What do you mean?

174
00:11:22,056 --> 00:11:23,933
I've heard troubling rumors.

175
00:11:24,016 --> 00:11:25,017
LADY OKURAKYO

176
00:11:25,101 --> 00:11:28,562
That you sacrificed every villager,

177
00:11:28,646 --> 00:11:33,359
women and children included,
to save your own skins.

178
00:11:34,360 --> 00:11:36,737
What do you mean, Lady Okurakyo?

179
00:11:36,821 --> 00:11:38,406
Are you pretending not to know?

180
00:11:40,116 --> 00:11:44,620
I heard Kudoyama was burned
to the ground, village and all.

181
00:11:44,703 --> 00:11:45,913
The whole village?!

182
00:11:47,540 --> 00:11:49,500
Hachi! Hachi!

183
00:11:51,210 --> 00:11:55,798
Can we really entrust
the fate of the Toyotomi

184
00:11:55,881 --> 00:11:58,092
to people like that?

185
00:12:00,511 --> 00:12:02,054
Is that true?

186
00:12:04,890 --> 00:12:06,392
They burned down all of Kudoyama?

187
00:12:06,475 --> 00:12:09,770
Who goes there? Do you know where you are?

188
00:12:09,854 --> 00:12:13,023
They serve under me. My apologies.

189
00:12:13,107 --> 00:12:16,152
Then the Tokugawa did it!
Approve the outpost!

190
00:12:16,235 --> 00:12:17,403
Silence!

191
00:12:17,486 --> 00:12:19,155
Siege or no siege,

192
00:12:19,905 --> 00:12:21,073
we'll avenge them!

193
00:12:21,157 --> 00:12:23,367
How dare they!

194
00:12:23,451 --> 00:12:26,996
Quite the fine ninja you have there.

195
00:12:27,538 --> 00:12:28,831
The outpost is forbidden!

196
00:12:29,915 --> 00:12:31,041
It'll only cause chaos.

197
00:12:34,962 --> 00:12:35,963
What the hell?!

198
00:12:37,965 --> 00:12:39,341
You stupid monkey!

199
00:12:39,425 --> 00:12:40,384
Ouch.

200
00:12:40,468 --> 00:12:42,136
Hey, I'm bleeding!

201
00:12:42,219 --> 00:12:45,681
For once, stop acting before you think!

202
00:12:50,936 --> 00:12:52,730
How can you all be so calm about this?

203
00:12:57,443 --> 00:12:59,987
The villagers
did everything they could to save us.

204
00:13:00,988 --> 00:13:02,114
And yet…

205
00:13:03,741 --> 00:13:04,783
How could I be calm?

206
00:13:07,495 --> 00:13:08,704
The Tokugawa's ninja…

207
00:13:09,997 --> 00:13:11,874
and Hattori Hanzo have taken

208
00:13:13,167 --> 00:13:15,377
precious things from me before.

209
00:13:19,256 --> 00:13:21,008
My name, Kamanosuke,

210
00:13:22,134 --> 00:13:24,762
was passed down from my father,
whom Hattori Hanzo killed.

211
00:13:29,850 --> 00:13:30,935
Here. You two.

212
00:13:32,686 --> 00:13:33,687
Sanada cord?

213
00:13:34,522 --> 00:13:36,899
Now's no time for us
to fight amongst ourselves.

214
00:13:42,696 --> 00:13:43,572
You're right.

215
00:13:44,615 --> 00:13:48,452
This cord is proof of our bond.

216
00:13:52,206 --> 00:13:53,707
Awful.

217
00:13:54,542 --> 00:13:55,751
Your blood tastes awful.

218
00:13:57,795 --> 00:13:58,796
Sasuke.

219
00:14:00,339 --> 00:14:01,882
Let's take down the Tokugawa together.

220
00:14:06,011 --> 00:14:06,845
You bet.

221
00:14:18,857 --> 00:14:20,150
Saizo, you've changed.

222
00:14:23,028 --> 00:14:26,156
I've never heard you use
the word "bond" before.

223
00:14:30,995 --> 00:14:34,498
Yuri, what will you do
when this war is over?

224
00:14:39,211 --> 00:14:40,296
What about you, Saizo?

225
00:14:41,630 --> 00:14:42,631
I…

226
00:14:47,595 --> 00:14:48,429
No.

227
00:14:49,847 --> 00:14:52,391
For now, let's focus on
defeating the Tokugawa.

228
00:14:55,394 --> 00:14:56,228
Yeah.

229
00:15:11,076 --> 00:15:12,912
All our men are assembled, then.

230
00:15:12,995 --> 00:15:16,916
With Lord Hidetada's arrival,
our position is secure.

231
00:15:18,417 --> 00:15:21,295
When I heard Sanada
had entered Osaka, I trembled.

232
00:15:22,463 --> 00:15:23,964
I've never forgotten

233
00:15:25,007 --> 00:15:26,926
the humiliation I suffered at Ueda.

234
00:15:27,760 --> 00:15:30,429
Osaka seems intent on
holding out in the castle,

235
00:15:31,180 --> 00:15:32,556
with no reinforcements coming.

236
00:15:33,849 --> 00:15:34,808
Foolish…

237
00:15:35,559 --> 00:15:38,687
A woman who knows nothing of war
holds the real power.

238
00:15:39,521 --> 00:15:41,315
Our victory is assured.

239
00:15:42,942 --> 00:15:45,778
At last, I'll take Sanada's head
with my own hands.

240
00:15:46,612 --> 00:15:47,613
Hidetada.

241
00:15:48,322 --> 00:15:50,741
Give Sanada hell.

242
00:15:50,824 --> 00:15:51,659
Yes, my lord!

243
00:15:52,743 --> 00:15:55,329
I have one concern.

244
00:15:56,372 --> 00:15:57,706
Speak, Hanzo.

245
00:15:58,290 --> 00:16:02,920
Even in this unfavorable position,
Sanada will devise some scheme.

246
00:16:03,712 --> 00:16:06,298
To be safe, I suggest sending my ninja--

247
00:16:06,382 --> 00:16:07,383
There's no need.

248
00:16:08,050 --> 00:16:09,927
I've already dispatched Lady Imbeyama.

249
00:16:10,719 --> 00:16:12,262
Lady Imbeyama?

250
00:16:12,846 --> 00:16:14,598
Your worries are unfounded.

251
00:16:15,307 --> 00:16:17,101
Whatever scheme Sanada devises…

252
00:16:19,103 --> 00:16:20,062
Bring it in.

253
00:16:20,854 --> 00:16:21,772
Yes, my lord.

254
00:16:23,315 --> 00:16:26,944
Suden, the item you requested has arrived.

255
00:16:27,027 --> 00:16:29,947
It's what the Ogosho requested.

256
00:16:42,876 --> 00:16:44,128
This is it…

257
00:16:45,587 --> 00:16:48,048
Well done, Hidetada!

258
00:16:48,716 --> 00:16:53,095
This monstrous being could serve as
the raw material for the ultimate ninja.

259
00:16:53,846 --> 00:16:55,180
Once it awakens,

260
00:16:55,848 --> 00:17:00,269
the Tokugawa will wield power
equal to a million-man army.

261
00:17:00,352 --> 00:17:01,311
MAGAMARU

262
00:17:01,395 --> 00:17:03,814
Hanzo, any other concerns?

263
00:17:07,860 --> 00:17:09,028
None, my lord.

264
00:17:09,111 --> 00:17:10,070
Good.

265
00:17:16,118 --> 00:17:17,953
Sanada has made no notable moves.

266
00:17:19,121 --> 00:17:21,165
The Tokugawa are truly unassailable.

267
00:17:21,999 --> 00:17:23,000
But…

268
00:17:24,084 --> 00:17:26,670
there's one more thing that concerns me.

269
00:17:30,049 --> 00:17:31,717
That monkey who got away…

270
00:17:32,926 --> 00:17:34,970
You mean Sasuke?

271
00:17:36,388 --> 00:17:39,767
You seemed to be close to him in Kudoyama.

272
00:17:40,476 --> 00:17:41,310
Yes.

273
00:17:41,810 --> 00:17:43,395
Then kill him.

274
00:17:44,605 --> 00:17:45,731
With your own hands.

275
00:17:47,024 --> 00:17:48,025
Understood?

276
00:17:48,942 --> 00:17:49,777
Yes, my lord.

277
00:17:55,741 --> 00:17:57,785
What are you doing out here
so late at night?

278
00:17:57,868 --> 00:17:59,453
Training for the coming battle.

279
00:18:01,538 --> 00:18:02,831
Let's do it again.

280
00:18:08,670 --> 00:18:09,713
Spe-cial?

281
00:18:11,757 --> 00:18:14,968
It means "special" in my native tongue.

282
00:18:16,845 --> 00:18:18,889
The two of them took quite a liking to it.

283
00:18:18,972 --> 00:18:21,433
I'll kick the soldier high into the air.

284
00:18:21,517 --> 00:18:23,018
As they go flying…

285
00:18:23,102 --> 00:18:25,187
I'll finish them off with shuriken.

286
00:18:25,270 --> 00:18:28,649
Don't finish him off!
That makes me sound like your assistant.

287
00:18:28,732 --> 00:18:31,527
-Leave him alive for a bit.
-Don't make it so complicated.

288
00:18:31,610 --> 00:18:33,195
-It's not complicated.
-Sasuke.

289
00:18:33,779 --> 00:18:34,696
Saizo.

290
00:18:35,280 --> 00:18:36,490
You fools!

291
00:18:37,950 --> 00:18:40,452
I hear you barged into the war council.

292
00:18:41,161 --> 00:18:43,163
You disgraced our lord!

293
00:18:44,248 --> 00:18:47,042
-We have no excuse.
-You needn't worry.

294
00:18:47,126 --> 00:18:49,211
Our lord is already taking action.

295
00:18:50,671 --> 00:18:54,299
He'll make Lady Yodo approve the outpost.

296
00:19:02,683 --> 00:19:05,102
Thank you for taking the trouble,

297
00:19:05,769 --> 00:19:07,104
Lady Okurakyo.

298
00:19:15,487 --> 00:19:19,116
One never knows
who's listening within the castle.

299
00:19:20,492 --> 00:19:21,743
You wish to obtain

300
00:19:22,452 --> 00:19:25,789
Lady Yodo's approval
for the outpost, don't you?

301
00:19:26,498 --> 00:19:28,375
I'm glad we're on the same page.

302
00:19:28,458 --> 00:19:29,543
Indeed.

303
00:19:30,419 --> 00:19:33,422
As the one closest to Lady Yodo,

304
00:19:34,214 --> 00:19:37,593
I may sway her if I speak on your behalf.

305
00:19:38,594 --> 00:19:39,511
But…

306
00:19:40,137 --> 00:19:43,724
I have no reason to help you,
Lord Sanada--

307
00:19:43,807 --> 00:19:45,100
No reason at all?

308
00:19:47,019 --> 00:19:51,190
You, who secretly sell the treasures
left by the Taiko to merchants

309
00:19:51,940 --> 00:19:54,234
to line your own pockets?

310
00:19:54,318 --> 00:19:55,652
What are you accusing me of?

311
00:19:55,736 --> 00:19:59,448
Our ninja have already searched
beneath the floor of your chambers.

312
00:20:09,833 --> 00:20:12,628
Imagine what would happen
if word got out in the castle.

313
00:20:16,548 --> 00:20:18,383
Let us make a deal.

314
00:20:22,804 --> 00:20:25,349
Damn that Sanada…

315
00:20:30,229 --> 00:20:31,396
What are you doing?!

316
00:20:39,321 --> 00:20:40,405
This is…

317
00:20:47,537 --> 00:20:49,498
Are you hurt?

318
00:20:54,086 --> 00:20:56,713
LADY IMBEYAMA

319
00:21:12,813 --> 00:21:14,106
Lady Yodo,

320
00:21:14,189 --> 00:21:18,360
I once again ask your permission

321
00:21:19,069 --> 00:21:20,737
to build an outpost south of the castle.

322
00:21:21,989 --> 00:21:23,156
What?

323
00:21:23,240 --> 00:21:28,036
Not one of us supports this plan.

324
00:21:33,250 --> 00:21:36,211
Is that truly so, Lady Okurakyo?

325
00:21:37,212 --> 00:21:38,255
What do you say?

326
00:21:42,050 --> 00:21:42,968
I…

327
00:22:08,285 --> 00:22:11,038
believe we should not build the outpost.

328
00:22:13,123 --> 00:22:18,587
Last night, this man used his ninja
to spy on the castle.

329
00:22:18,670 --> 00:22:19,546
Please, wait!

330
00:22:19,629 --> 00:22:22,382
What's more,
I hear he bought his escape from Kudoyama

331
00:22:23,091 --> 00:22:25,594
by sacrificing the villagers

332
00:22:26,178 --> 00:22:28,055
to the Tokugawa.

333
00:22:29,139 --> 00:22:30,724
That can't possibly be true!

334
00:22:30,807 --> 00:22:32,726
Do not listen to him!

335
00:22:33,310 --> 00:22:35,353
He may have defected to the Tokugawa.

336
00:22:37,439 --> 00:22:38,440
This man…

337
00:22:39,107 --> 00:22:41,401
is a demon who will lead

338
00:22:41,485 --> 00:22:43,153
the Toyotomi to ruin!

339
00:22:55,624 --> 00:22:57,459
Lady Okurakyo! Help!

340
00:22:59,169 --> 00:23:00,170
Lady Okurakyo!

341
00:23:00,754 --> 00:23:01,963
What's wrong?!

342
00:23:02,964 --> 00:23:07,135
Is it true you sent your ninja
to investigate the castle?

343
00:23:09,096 --> 00:23:09,930
Yes.

344
00:23:29,366 --> 00:23:30,200
I've had it!

345
00:23:31,409 --> 00:23:32,577
I'm done with this!

346
00:23:34,246 --> 00:23:36,331
We can't attack or build the outpost.

347
00:23:36,414 --> 00:23:38,250
How the hell are we
supposed to win like this?

348
00:23:39,126 --> 00:23:41,670
Sasuke, calm down!

349
00:23:41,753 --> 00:23:44,256
I came all this way to take down Ieyasu.

350
00:23:44,339 --> 00:23:46,466
I didn't come all this way
to fight a losing battle.

351
00:23:46,550 --> 00:23:48,885
But the Toyotomi have made their decision.

352
00:23:50,428 --> 00:23:52,139
Then this is where I leave.

353
00:23:54,808 --> 00:23:57,227
We agreed I'd only come
as far as Osaka, remember?

354
00:23:57,936 --> 00:23:59,938
I'll take Hanzo and Ieyasu's heads myself.

355
00:24:00,021 --> 00:24:02,649
-Don't be ridiculous.
-Give it back.

356
00:24:02,732 --> 00:24:04,818
I'll come up with a good plan, I promise!

357
00:24:05,527 --> 00:24:09,364
What's the point of thinking up plans
if we can't convince Lady Yodo?

358
00:24:10,448 --> 00:24:13,243
I'm frustrated too!

359
00:24:13,326 --> 00:24:16,371
But we have to keep thinking,
no matter what!

360
00:24:20,167 --> 00:24:21,751
What can you do on your own?

361
00:24:22,502 --> 00:24:23,712
Just hang in there for now.

362
00:24:27,465 --> 00:24:28,383
Shut up.

363
00:24:29,176 --> 00:24:30,427
Don't order me around.

364
00:24:30,510 --> 00:24:31,595
Stop, both of you.

365
00:24:36,141 --> 00:24:38,935
I was a fool to put any faith in you.

366
00:24:40,562 --> 00:24:42,397
Don't ever show your face again.

367
00:24:59,623 --> 00:25:01,541
Shouldn't we stop him?

368
00:25:11,426 --> 00:25:14,387
Sasuke! I really want to get stronger!

369
00:25:14,971 --> 00:25:17,098
-That's why I want to learn more--
-If you're serious…

370
00:25:19,309 --> 00:25:20,977
stop relying on others.

371
00:25:24,814 --> 00:25:26,775
Figure it out on your own.

372
00:25:44,000 --> 00:25:48,004
Lady Okurakyo
has been bedridden ever since.

373
00:25:48,838 --> 00:25:49,923
I see…

374
00:25:51,341 --> 00:25:53,343
Is this as far as we can go?

375
00:25:58,848 --> 00:25:59,766
Everyone…

376
00:26:01,726 --> 00:26:02,769
can I have a moment?

377
00:26:09,359 --> 00:26:12,028
Hey, where do I go to find Ieyasu?

378
00:26:12,112 --> 00:26:13,530
What are you talking about?

379
00:26:16,116 --> 00:26:19,494
Hey, hey! Where can I find Ieyasu?

380
00:26:19,577 --> 00:26:21,288
Don't get involved.

381
00:26:21,371 --> 00:26:22,580
Who is he? Who?

382
00:26:26,251 --> 00:26:29,087
I'm starving…

383
00:26:57,407 --> 00:26:58,241
Here.

384
00:26:59,367 --> 00:27:00,327
Eat up.

385
00:27:04,748 --> 00:27:05,582
Is it good?

386
00:27:08,293 --> 00:27:10,378
Hey! That's ours!

387
00:27:11,212 --> 00:27:13,173
Fine! I'll pay, all right?

388
00:27:13,965 --> 00:27:16,801
Old Yukimura promised me a hefty reward…

389
00:27:21,389 --> 00:27:22,307
I don't have it on me.

390
00:27:23,850 --> 00:27:25,268
Damn it.

391
00:27:25,935 --> 00:27:27,520
I left it at the castle!

392
00:27:27,604 --> 00:27:30,690
You thief! Just come with us! You too!

393
00:27:30,774 --> 00:27:32,525
-The kid's not involved!
-Shut up!

394
00:27:32,609 --> 00:27:33,777
I'll pay for it!

395
00:27:34,277 --> 00:27:35,445
Okuni?

396
00:27:36,529 --> 00:27:38,406
It's been a while, Sasuke.

397
00:27:41,076 --> 00:27:42,535
You're going after Ieyasu alone?

398
00:27:42,619 --> 00:27:43,453
Yeah.

399
00:27:44,037 --> 00:27:46,206
Isn't that far too reckless?

400
00:27:47,040 --> 00:27:48,541
That's what they said, too.

401
00:27:49,584 --> 00:27:51,961
But they just can't do anything alone.

402
00:27:52,629 --> 00:27:55,298
Maybe that's true
for someone like you, Sasuke.

403
00:27:57,175 --> 00:27:59,636
I heard what happened at Kudoyama.

404
00:28:00,804 --> 00:28:03,181
I'm just glad you survived, at least.

405
00:28:04,307 --> 00:28:07,394
But how am I supposed to
live on my own now?

406
00:28:08,520 --> 00:28:09,354
That's…

407
00:28:09,437 --> 00:28:13,316
Not everyone is as strong as you, Sasuke.

408
00:28:17,737 --> 00:28:19,864
Maybe I went a little too far.

409
00:28:20,365 --> 00:28:21,408
What?

410
00:28:21,491 --> 00:28:23,743
I mean…

411
00:28:25,954 --> 00:28:27,580
how you live your life…

412
00:28:28,373 --> 00:28:30,458
That's not for someone else
to decide, right?

413
00:28:33,545 --> 00:28:35,588
LOCAL SPECIALTY
DANGO

414
00:28:35,672 --> 00:28:38,174
-Where are you going?
-There's somewhere I need to stop first.

415
00:28:39,134 --> 00:28:41,386
Besides, Ieyasu will be
coming this way anyway, right?

416
00:28:42,095 --> 00:28:44,305
I'll lie low around here for a while.

417
00:28:46,599 --> 00:28:47,892
Do you have somewhere to stay?

418
00:28:49,602 --> 00:28:50,895
A place to stay…

419
00:28:52,439 --> 00:28:56,818
If you don't, why not stay at my inn?

420
00:29:06,578 --> 00:29:09,414
What brings you here
at this hour, Hideyori?

421
00:29:10,415 --> 00:29:11,916
As Lord Sanada said,

422
00:29:13,084 --> 00:29:15,962
we should build an outpost
south of the castle.

423
00:29:16,629 --> 00:29:17,630
What?!

424
00:29:18,339 --> 00:29:19,299
That's our

425
00:29:20,633 --> 00:29:24,137
one-in-a-million shot at winning this war.

426
00:29:28,850 --> 00:29:31,644
Pretend to be Lord Hideyori?!

427
00:29:32,353 --> 00:29:36,733
I've studied his mannerisms,
and we look exactly alike.

428
00:29:37,609 --> 00:29:41,654
If I speak as Lord Hideyori,
I should be able to sway Lady Yodo.

429
00:29:42,363 --> 00:29:46,201
Could such a thing really work?

430
00:29:47,118 --> 00:29:48,036
All right!

431
00:29:49,078 --> 00:29:50,288
-Let's do it!
-Yeah.

432
00:29:51,289 --> 00:29:52,373
Shakespeare said,

433
00:29:53,208 --> 00:29:56,669
"Then I defy you, stars!"

434
00:29:57,796 --> 00:30:00,423
We'll strike at the Hour of the Boar,
while Lord Hideyori sleeps.

435
00:30:01,299 --> 00:30:05,428
Everyone, keep watch
in case Lord Hideyori wakes up.

436
00:30:11,684 --> 00:30:14,062
There's no sign
of Lord Hideyori waking up.

437
00:30:14,145 --> 00:30:15,605
What a relief.

438
00:30:17,899 --> 00:30:19,150
Kakei, what's wrong?

439
00:30:21,820 --> 00:30:25,990
This plan was Lord Yukimura's idea, right?

440
00:30:26,825 --> 00:30:30,411
No one but Lord Yukimura
could come up with such a bold plan.

441
00:30:31,371 --> 00:30:33,957
Then why keep it secret
from everyone else?

442
00:30:35,416 --> 00:30:38,711
Saizo and Yuri
would be better suited to keep watch.

443
00:30:40,588 --> 00:30:42,924
I guess he trusts us.

444
00:30:43,716 --> 00:30:48,304
But what happens if this plan fails?

445
00:30:48,388 --> 00:30:49,722
That's obvious.

446
00:30:50,223 --> 00:30:52,350
We're impersonating Lord Hideyori.

447
00:30:53,101 --> 00:30:54,769
If we fail…

448
00:30:55,562 --> 00:30:57,438
we'll all be beheaded.

449
00:30:59,315 --> 00:31:00,275
Beheaded?

450
00:31:01,067 --> 00:31:05,154
What's wrong, Hideyori? You seem like
a completely different person.

451
00:31:06,155 --> 00:31:08,032
I'm no longer a child.

452
00:31:09,868 --> 00:31:11,619
Shouldn't we trust Lord Sanada's plan?

453
00:31:12,412 --> 00:31:14,330
He's given the Tokugawa trouble twice,

454
00:31:14,414 --> 00:31:16,875
unlike us, who know so little of war.

455
00:31:22,672 --> 00:31:27,427
So you've grown into a fine lord
without me realizing it.

456
00:31:30,221 --> 00:31:32,265
I understand your feelings.

457
00:31:36,728 --> 00:31:37,562
Then…

458
00:31:40,773 --> 00:31:41,774
However…

459
00:31:42,817 --> 00:31:45,945
such an important decision
cannot be made at once.

460
00:31:46,946 --> 00:31:47,906
What?

461
00:31:47,989 --> 00:31:51,284
Tomorrow, we'll discuss it again
with the retainers.

462
00:31:51,367 --> 00:31:52,660
No!

463
00:31:52,744 --> 00:31:54,412
You must decide right here, right now!

464
00:31:54,495 --> 00:31:56,539
Why are you in such a hurry?

465
00:31:57,957 --> 00:31:58,833
That's because…

466
00:31:59,500 --> 00:32:02,170
Hey, what are you doing here?

467
00:32:03,212 --> 00:32:04,213
You…!

468
00:32:05,006 --> 00:32:07,425
You insolent wretch!
Get out of here at once!

469
00:32:07,508 --> 00:32:09,594
I hate being ordered around.

470
00:32:10,303 --> 00:32:11,763
It's not my problem anymore.

471
00:32:14,724 --> 00:32:16,351
Yeah, you're Daisuke.

472
00:32:16,893 --> 00:32:17,894
Daisuke?

473
00:32:17,977 --> 00:32:19,145
No, that's…

474
00:32:19,771 --> 00:32:23,691
Sorry about earlier, telling you
to handle things yourself and all.

475
00:32:23,775 --> 00:32:26,527
Not everyone has to make it on their own.

476
00:32:26,611 --> 00:32:28,863
-What are you talking about?
-Shut it, old hag.

477
00:32:28,947 --> 00:32:29,864
Old hag?!

478
00:32:30,448 --> 00:32:31,574
What I meant was,

479
00:32:32,283 --> 00:32:34,410
you should decide
how you want to live for yourself.

480
00:32:35,870 --> 00:32:37,372
-Is something the matter?
-Crap!

481
00:32:38,247 --> 00:32:39,082
Well, I'm off.

482
00:32:39,707 --> 00:32:42,168
I just stopped by
while collecting my reward.

483
00:32:52,762 --> 00:32:53,596
Is Hideyori here?

484
00:32:54,514 --> 00:32:57,725
See? There's no one here. I'm Hideyori.

485
00:32:57,809 --> 00:32:59,519
Let's hurry back to your room, Mother…

486
00:32:59,602 --> 00:33:01,854
Hideyori! If you're here, answer me!

487
00:33:08,319 --> 00:33:09,320
Mother…

488
00:33:13,032 --> 00:33:14,117
Who are you?!

489
00:33:14,200 --> 00:33:15,201
Hideyori!

490
00:33:17,370 --> 00:33:19,872
No doubt about it.
That mole! It's Hideyori!

491
00:33:22,166 --> 00:33:23,626
You're ninja, aren't you?

492
00:33:24,627 --> 00:33:27,380
Yukimura put you up to this, didn't he?

493
00:33:27,463 --> 00:33:29,090
No! I did this on my own.

494
00:33:29,173 --> 00:33:30,216
Guards! Guards!

495
00:33:31,175 --> 00:33:34,429
There's an intruder!
Seize him! Guards! Guards!

496
00:33:35,054 --> 00:33:36,097
You fools!

497
00:33:36,681 --> 00:33:39,267
I can't believe
you impersonated Lord Hideyori…

498
00:33:40,476 --> 00:33:41,811
My apologies!

499
00:33:42,562 --> 00:33:44,522
And why didn't the rest of you stop him?

500
00:33:45,982 --> 00:33:48,234
What happened to that insolent ninja?

501
00:33:48,317 --> 00:33:49,152
You mean Sasuke?

502
00:33:50,361 --> 00:33:51,487
Tomorrow,

503
00:33:52,280 --> 00:33:54,782
judgment will be passed
on everyone involved in this.

504
00:33:55,700 --> 00:33:56,617
Well…

505
00:33:58,411 --> 00:34:01,330
I'm sure it'll mean beheading.

506
00:34:04,125 --> 00:34:05,793
Bring that monkey here, too.

507
00:34:06,878 --> 00:34:07,962
Don't try to escape.

508
00:34:14,844 --> 00:34:16,471
I'll bring Sasuke back.

509
00:34:16,554 --> 00:34:17,472
That's unnecessary.

510
00:34:18,222 --> 00:34:22,894
It's my duty to take responsibility
for my retainers' failures.

511
00:34:24,020 --> 00:34:24,896
My lord!

512
00:34:45,500 --> 00:34:46,501
I'm coming, too.

513
00:34:57,720 --> 00:34:58,846
Sasuke?

514
00:35:09,023 --> 00:35:10,858
You're surprisingly naive.

515
00:35:28,876 --> 00:35:30,837
What the hell are these guys? Stay back!

516
00:35:43,808 --> 00:35:45,560
Not bad.

517
00:35:47,937 --> 00:35:49,021
But…

518
00:35:49,105 --> 00:35:51,899
if this is giving you trouble,

519
00:35:51,983 --> 00:35:54,652
you'll never take the Ogosho's head.

520
00:36:01,826 --> 00:36:03,035
Sasuke…

521
00:36:15,548 --> 00:36:16,757
Enchain.

522
00:36:22,430 --> 00:36:24,515
Ninja are despised

523
00:36:25,975 --> 00:36:28,895
and used as pawns by the Toyotomi,
only to die in the end.

524
00:36:29,854 --> 00:36:32,023
That's your fate.

525
00:36:34,817 --> 00:36:35,943
Do it.

526
00:36:37,028 --> 00:36:38,404
Join the Tokugawa.

527
00:36:48,539 --> 00:36:49,457
Stay away from Saizo!

528
00:36:50,499 --> 00:36:52,752
Do you really think
you can protect him like this?

529
00:37:00,843 --> 00:37:01,844
Are you all right?

530
00:37:06,891 --> 00:37:07,808
Saizo?

531
00:37:12,313 --> 00:37:14,148
Would my head not suffice?

532
00:37:14,232 --> 00:37:15,107
Enough!

533
00:37:29,205 --> 00:37:30,289
Father!

534
00:37:33,960 --> 00:37:35,044
Can I speak with you?

535
00:37:36,420 --> 00:37:38,381
You needn't be so formal.

536
00:37:39,548 --> 00:37:40,549
But…

537
00:37:42,343 --> 00:37:46,472
I just wanted to talk to you.

538
00:37:48,808 --> 00:37:50,851
You, who bears the same face as me…

539
00:37:54,897 --> 00:37:56,440
the son of Yukimura.

540
00:37:57,733 --> 00:37:58,693
Why…

541
00:38:00,027 --> 00:38:02,113
do we look so much alike?

542
00:38:03,823 --> 00:38:04,865
That's…

543
00:38:06,575 --> 00:38:07,702
Well, never mind that.

544
00:38:10,037 --> 00:38:14,041
Still, you've certainly caused
quite a stir.

545
00:38:15,960 --> 00:38:19,213
This whole affair was my doing.

546
00:38:20,589 --> 00:38:22,216
Please, let me bear the blame alone!

547
00:38:24,969 --> 00:38:26,595
Do you not fear death?

548
00:38:29,140 --> 00:38:30,725
I wish to decide how I live…

549
00:38:33,853 --> 00:38:35,479
for myself.

550
00:38:39,066 --> 00:38:40,568
I'd rather die with pride…

551
00:38:42,862 --> 00:38:45,990
as Sanada Yukimura's son

552
00:38:47,908 --> 00:38:49,368
than live on like this.

553
00:38:58,753 --> 00:39:00,671
After causing such a commotion,

554
00:39:02,131 --> 00:39:04,008
don't you think it's too convenient

555
00:39:05,051 --> 00:39:06,761
to punish only you?

556
00:39:06,844 --> 00:39:07,887
Even so…

557
00:39:08,554 --> 00:39:10,389
My father and his men…

558
00:39:12,516 --> 00:39:13,893
will surely be

559
00:39:15,186 --> 00:39:16,854
an asset to the Toyotomi.

560
00:39:16,937 --> 00:39:20,858
I doubt that insolent ninja who barged
into the war council will be of any use.

561
00:39:29,075 --> 00:39:30,326
One last question.

562
00:39:33,454 --> 00:39:34,830
What kind of man…

563
00:39:37,041 --> 00:39:38,250
is Sanada Yukimura?

564
00:39:47,885 --> 00:39:49,178
Had times been different…

565
00:39:52,056 --> 00:39:53,724
he would have ruled the realm.

566
00:39:56,435 --> 00:39:57,770
Though I share his blood…

567
00:39:59,980 --> 00:40:01,607
I'm nowhere near his equal.

568
00:40:04,693 --> 00:40:05,778
And there are things…

569
00:40:07,863 --> 00:40:09,698
even Lord Hideyori cannot do…

570
00:40:12,993 --> 00:40:14,203
that he can.

571
00:40:21,627 --> 00:40:22,545
Enough.

572
00:40:24,213 --> 00:40:25,172
You may leave.

573
00:40:26,924 --> 00:40:27,800
Yes, my lord!

574
00:41:10,759 --> 00:41:12,344
To think…

575
00:41:13,512 --> 00:41:15,848
you'd scheme against Lady Yodo…

576
00:41:17,308 --> 00:41:19,852
You're prepared to face
the consequences, I trust?

577
00:41:20,895 --> 00:41:25,941
A ninja commander of your caliber
is too valuable to lose, Lord Sanada.

578
00:41:26,650 --> 00:41:28,986
But it can't be helped.

579
00:41:30,404 --> 00:41:34,283
Lord Hideyori and Lady Yodo are here!

580
00:41:52,760 --> 00:41:54,762
Regarding the punishment of Lord Sanada…

581
00:41:56,639 --> 00:41:59,391
and his retainers
for yesterday's incident…

582
00:42:01,810 --> 00:42:02,895
as for his retainers,

583
00:42:04,230 --> 00:42:05,731
all offenses…

584
00:42:08,275 --> 00:42:09,610
shall be overlooked.

585
00:42:13,656 --> 00:42:17,493
A lord should bear responsibility
for his retainers' failures.

586
00:42:20,579 --> 00:42:21,997
Sanada Yukimura.

587
00:42:22,581 --> 00:42:23,415
Yes!

588
00:42:24,959 --> 00:42:27,169
I'm prepared.

589
00:42:27,836 --> 00:42:29,588
Before I pass judgment,

590
00:42:30,172 --> 00:42:34,552
tell me once more what you think
of our strategy for defending the castle.

591
00:42:37,054 --> 00:42:38,681
If you support our plan

592
00:42:39,598 --> 00:42:41,433
and continue to serve us,

593
00:42:42,309 --> 00:42:43,727
I'll overlook this incident.

594
00:42:45,145 --> 00:42:46,063
But if you refuse,

595
00:42:47,231 --> 00:42:49,358
I'll have no choice
but to regard it as treason.

596
00:42:51,068 --> 00:42:55,155
Do we stand any chance of winning
if we continue to hold out in the castle?

597
00:42:59,702 --> 00:43:00,744
None.

598
00:43:03,372 --> 00:43:04,206
I see.

599
00:43:05,499 --> 00:43:07,960
Then I shall pass judgment.

600
00:43:11,338 --> 00:43:12,298
Sanada.

601
00:43:13,007 --> 00:43:13,882
Yes.

602
00:43:16,093 --> 00:43:18,012
Build an outpost to the southeast.

603
00:43:22,641 --> 00:43:24,184
You will be responsible

604
00:43:25,686 --> 00:43:27,187
for driving back the Tokugawa.

605
00:43:27,688 --> 00:43:29,940
Hideyori! What are you saying?

606
00:43:30,024 --> 00:43:33,527
We can't win this war
by meeting them head-on.

607
00:43:34,403 --> 00:43:37,740
We need people like them,
who aren't bound by convention.

608
00:43:37,823 --> 00:43:40,909
But after what they did to you yesterday…

609
00:43:42,328 --> 00:43:43,495
Another impostor…?

610
00:43:44,288 --> 00:43:46,498
-Hideyori should have a mole there--
-I do have a mole.

611
00:43:48,959 --> 00:43:51,670
Stop treating me like a child!

612
00:43:52,838 --> 00:43:54,632
I am the head of the Toyotomi clan!

613
00:43:55,215 --> 00:43:57,760
And I say that I trust them

614
00:43:58,552 --> 00:44:00,638
and approve the construction
of the outpost.

615
00:44:06,685 --> 00:44:08,187
I'll decide how I live…

616
00:44:09,813 --> 00:44:10,939
for myself.

617
00:44:16,987 --> 00:44:19,281
What kind of trick did you pull?

618
00:44:20,574 --> 00:44:21,742
A report!

619
00:44:24,036 --> 00:44:25,120
I bring urgent news!

620
00:44:25,204 --> 00:44:27,206
The Tokugawa forces have

621
00:44:27,289 --> 00:44:30,125
begun marching from Nijo Castle
in Kyoto toward Osaka!

622
00:44:30,793 --> 00:44:31,794
Excuse me!

623
00:44:40,969 --> 00:44:41,887
Mother…

624
00:44:44,014 --> 00:44:45,474
we must prepare ourselves.

625
00:44:56,276 --> 00:44:57,111
Yukimura!

626
00:44:58,612 --> 00:44:59,446
Yes!

627
00:45:01,031 --> 00:45:02,032
Don't fail us.

628
00:45:03,450 --> 00:45:04,868
We will win this war,

629
00:45:06,120 --> 00:45:07,079
no matter what!

630
00:45:51,790 --> 00:45:53,333
You all made it back safely!

631
00:46:17,399 --> 00:46:21,487
Take them to the Ogosho.

632
00:46:21,570 --> 00:46:22,654
Yes, my lord!

633
00:46:27,117 --> 00:46:30,871
Subtitle translation by: Sayo Takada

634
00:46:30,954 --> 00:46:32,873
THIS DRAMA IS A WORK OF FICTION
